  "_commit": {
    "id": "bcc5165be1ace4aea4cc700232afc0922cb3bd6f",
    "author": "Herv\u00e9 Pag\u00e8s <hpages.on.github@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Herv\u00e9 Pag\u00e8s <hpages.on.github@gmail.com>",
    "message": "annotate 1.91.1: Deprecate findNeighbors() and related helpers\n\nfindNeighbors() needs access to a CHROMLOC package (i.e. humanCHRLOC,\nmouseCHROMLOC, or ratCHRLOC) in order to work but these packages have\nbeen deprecated in BioC 3.23 and removed in BioC 3.24, which means\nthat, starting with BioC 3.24, the function can no longer be used.\nSo the function is now formally deprecated together with its various\nhelper functions (which BTW should have never been exported in the first\nplace).\n\nThere's no exact replacement for the function but the man page now shows\na GRanges-based approach to finding the genomic neighbors of a given gene.\n",
    "time": 1794367175
  },
